 "standard_code": "A-REI.B.3",
 "standard_url": "https://www.thecorestandards.org/Math/Content/HSA/REI/B/3/",
 "standard_text": "Solve linear equations and inequalities in one variable, including equations with coefficients represented by letters.",
 "meta_desc": "Free Algebra 1 multi-step equations worksheets (A-REI.B.3): distribute and combine like terms, parentheses on both sides, equations with fractions and decimals, and writing equations for word problems. 100 questions with an answer key.",
 "key_big": "Clear parentheses, clear fractions, collect like terms, then divide.",
 "key_sub": "Do the same thing to both sides, and check by substituting your answer.",
 "body_html": "<h2>How it works</h2><p>Solve a multi-step equation in this order: <b>clear parentheses</b> (distribute), <b>clear fractions or decimals</b> (multiply every term by the same number), <b>collect</b> the variable terms on one side and the numbers on the other, then <b>divide</b>. Do the same thing to both sides each time, and check by substituting your answer.</p><p>A minus sign in front of parentheses changes the sign of <b>every</b> term inside: −2(<i>x</i> − 3) = −2<i>x</i> + 6.</p><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>Solve 4(2<i>x</i> + 1) − 3(<i>x</i> − 2) = 25.</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>Distribute: 8<i>x</i> + 4 − 3<i>x</i> + 6 = 25.</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>Combine: 5<i>x</i> + 10 = 25.</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>5<i>x</i> = 15.</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: <i>x</i> = 3</p></div><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>Solve <span class='fr'><span class='fn'><i>x</i></span><span class='fd'>3</span></span> + <span class='fr'><span class='fn'><i>x</i></span><span class='fd'>4</span></span> = 14.</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>Multiply every term by 12: 4<i>x</i> + 3<i>x</i> = 168.</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>7<i>x</i> = 168.</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: <i>x</i> = 24</p></div><div class='sn-ex'><span class='sn-ex-t'>Example</span><p class='sn-ex-q'>Solve 0.3<i>x</i> + 1.2 = 0.1<i>x</i> + 2.</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>Multiply by 10: 3<i>x</i> + 12 = <i>x</i> + 20.</p><p class='sn-ex-s'>2<i>x</i> = 8.</p><p class='sn-ex-a'>Answer: <i>x</i> = 4</p></div><h2>Common mistakes</h2><ul><li>Changing only the first sign after a minus: −3(<i>x</i> − 2) is −3<i>x</i> + 6, not −3<i>x</i> − 6.</li><li>Distributing to the first term only: 4(2<i>x</i> + 1) is 8<i>x</i> + 4, not 8<i>x</i> + 1.</li><li>Multiplying only the fractions by the common denominator. Every term, on both sides, must be multiplied.</li><li>Stopping at 5<i>x</i> = 15. Divide to get <i>x</i> on its own.</li></ul>",
 "faq": [
  {
   "q": "How do you solve multi-step equations?",
   "a": "Distribute to clear parentheses, multiply to clear fractions or decimals, collect the variable terms on one side and the numbers on the other, then divide by the coefficient."
  },
  {
   "q": "How do you solve an equation with fractions?",
   "a": "Multiply every term on both sides by a common denominator. The fractions disappear and you solve the equation that is left."
  },
  {
   "q": "What happens to a minus sign in front of parentheses?",
   "a": "It changes the sign of every term inside: −(x − 4) = −x + 4."
  },
  {
   "q": "How do I check my answer?",
   "a": "Substitute it into the original equation. Both sides should give the same number."
  }
 ],
